AB  - Binary ethanol-H2 gas samples were measured by an innovative mobile sensor system for the alcohol control in the respiratory air. The measurements were performed by a gas sensor operated by cyclic variation of the working temperature at the sensor head. The evaluation of the data, using an updated version of the evaluation procedure ProSens, results in a very good substance identification and concentration determination of the components of the gas mixture. The relative analysis errors were in all cases less than 9%.
