KW  - Flexible microwave sensor
KW  - non-intrusive liquid detection
KW  - PEDOT:PSS material
KW  - split ring resonator
KW  - SENSOR
AB  - Intrinsically conducting polymers render a promising alternative to conventional copper-based electronic devices, offering a solution to implement flexible devices. This study presents a non-intrusive liquid sensing setup comprised of a multilayer flexible split ring resonator as a sensing tag on a 50-Ohms-matched microstrip structure. The conductive layer of the proposed tag is fabricated using a flexible organic PEDOT:PSS material and highly conductive inorganic Ag nanowires to enhance the conductivity and flexibility of the polymeric structure. The fabricated sensor operates at the resonant frequency of 3.45 GHz with a resonant amplitude of -19.91 dB. The liquid sensing capability of the unbent tag is investigated using different volumes of standard liquids, including deionized water, ethanol, methanol, and isopropyl alcohol. Then, the proposed tag is wrapped around the exterior wall of a liquid container to demonstrate its sensing performance under bent condition. The integration of flexible and contactless microwave-based sensing capabilities makes the tag versatile and adaptable for various potential applications ranging from wearable sensors in healthcare monitoring to non-intrusive material characterization in chemical and pharmaceutical industries.
